# What must never enter the build context.
#
# Both build stages run `COPY . /app`, so anything reachable from here lands in
# an image layer — and layers survive the final stage not copying them forward.
# An image exported, pushed, or handed to anybody would otherwise carry the
# key-encryption key sitting next to the sealed documents it opens, which is
# precisely the arrangement D12 exists to prevent.

# The key. Losing it loses the vault; leaking it loses the vault to somebody
# else (D12).
keys
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.age
*.gpg

# Sealed documents. The container reads these from a mounted volume at runtime,
# never from the image.
storage
uploads
documents
vault-data
data

# Database passwords, the session signing secret, the lot.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Backups, dumps and anything else that is a copy of the vault.
backups
*.dump
*.sql.gz
pgdata
postgres-data

# Build output and dependencies: rebuilt inside the image.
.react-router
build
node_modules
coverage

# Not needed to build or run, and keeps the context small.
.git
.github
.claude
.serena
.impeccable
docs
tasks
graphify-out
README.md
*.log
